From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 03:28:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 171/184] Sega CD: keep the desktop's settings on I:, which
 both boots share

EmuTOS keeps EMUDESK.INF on the boot drive. On this machine that is C:,
a RAM disk rebuilt from the disc or from the cartridge ROM every time
the console starts, so Options > Save Desktop wrote the background
colour, the window positions and the icon layout somewhere that ceased
to exist at power-off. The setting could be changed and never kept.

I: is the console's own internal backup RAM: soldered down, battery
backed, eight kilobytes, and present however the machine was booted --
from the disc, or from a cartridge in Mode 1. It is the one writable
volume both boot paths share, so a setting saved from either is there
for the other.

So INF_PERSIST_NAME, defined for MACHINE_SEGACD as I:\EMUDESK.INF.
Saving goes there. Reading tries it first and falls back to the boot
drive, so a console whose I: has never been formatted still gets the
defaults that shipped on the disc.

Verified in the emulator: with a FAT12 volume seeded on the internal
backup RAM carrying an EMUDESK.INF that omits one drive icon, the
desktop comes up with that icon gone -- 1006 pixels different from the
same boot without it. (Persistence itself cannot be shown headless:
Genesis Plus GX wipes the internal BRAM at load unless it finds Sega's
own format footer in the last 64 bytes, and refuses to write the file
back without it. That is the emulator enforcing Sega's layout, not the
hardware.)
---
 desk/deskapp.c   | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 include/config.h | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+)

diff --git a/desk/deskapp.c b/desk/deskapp.c
index 1564304..2f57a3f 100644
--- a/desk/deskapp.c
+++ b/desk/deskapp.c
@@ -682,6 +682,18 @@ static void read_inf_file(char *infbuf)
     LONG ret;
     char inf_file_name[sizeof(INF_FILE_NAME)];
 
+#ifdef INF_PERSIST_NAME
+    /* The settings the user saved, on a volume that survives the power
+     * going off, before the copy that shipped with the system. An
+     * absent or unformatted persistent drive just falls through. */
+    ret = dos_load_file(INF_PERSIST_NAME, SIZE_SHELBUF-CPDATA_LEN-1, infbuf);
+    if (ret > 0L)
+    {
+        infbuf[ret] = '\0';
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
+
     strcpy(inf_file_name, INF_FILE_NAME);
     inf_file_name[0] += G.g_stdrv;      /* Adjust drive letter  */
 
@@ -1046,8 +1058,15 @@ static void save_to_disk(char *buf, WORD len)
     if (fun_alert(1, STSVINF) != 1)
         return;
 
+#ifdef INF_PERSIST_NAME
+    /* Saved settings go where they will still be after the power has
+     * been off, and where the other boot path will also find them --
+     * not to the boot drive, which here is a RAM disk. */
+    strcpy(inf_file_name, INF_PERSIST_NAME);
+#else
     strcpy(inf_file_name, INF_FILE_NAME);
     inf_file_name[0] += G.g_stdrv;  /* Adjust drive letter  */
+#endif
 
     while(1)
     {
diff --git a/include/config.h b/include/config.h
index aa8bcf6..e61cba1 100644
--- a/include/config.h
+++ b/include/config.h
@@ -632,6 +632,26 @@
 # ifndef CONF_WITH_READ_INF
 #  define CONF_WITH_READ_INF 0
 # endif
+# ifndef INF_PERSIST_NAME
+   /* Where the desktop's own settings live.
+    *
+    * EmuTOS keeps EMUDESK.INF on the boot drive, and on this machine
+    * the boot drive is C:, a RAM disk rebuilt from the disc or from the
+    * cartridge ROM on every start. Anything saved there is gone at
+    * power-off, so the background colour, the window positions and the
+    * icon layout could be changed but never kept.
+    *
+    * I: is the console's own internal backup RAM: soldered down,
+    * battery-backed, eight kilobytes, and present no matter which way
+    * the machine was booted -- from the disc, or from a cartridge in
+    * Mode 1. It is the one volume both boot paths share and neither can
+    * lose, which makes it the right home for a setting the owner
+    * expects to still be there tomorrow.
+    *
+    * Reading falls back to the boot drive, so a console whose I: has
+    * never been formatted still gets the shipped defaults. */
+#  define INF_PERSIST_NAME "I:\\EMUDESK.INF"
+# endif
 # ifndef CONF_STRAM_SIZE
 #  define CONF_STRAM_SIZE (384UL*1024)
 # endif
